{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361494-what-s-on-your-exalted-bingo-card","id":1361494,"title":"What's on your Exalted bingo card?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-17T09:22:47-08:00","id":1361494,"title":"What's on your Exalted bingo card?","content":"So lately I've been a little called out by the fianc\u00e9e on a few behaviour patterns of my characters and plot elements in my games and she joked about getting bingo cards made.<br /> Some of it was pretty obvious even to me, I do enjoy masked secret societies and characters who won't quite lie about their backstories, but they will sprinkle a bit of Obi Wan truth in there so that people think they know what's going on when really they don't. Most recently I had it pointed out to me that when my characters fight they are often exceedingly vicious to the point that so far 3 of my third edition characters have bitten people.<br /> <br /> So, what would your bingo card say of your deeds?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":1115,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","user":"The Hug Ninja","date":". 01-17-2020, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T09:58:46-08:00","id":1361512,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>My characters tend to be eccentrics who shock others with their unexpected behaviour, be it in a good or a bad way.</li> <li>They will often be zealous in their beliefs and motivations, usually to a fault.</li> <li>In terms of party dynamics, I usually try to bridge the gap between the 2 extremes in the group. I do this either by being a voice of reason, or by acting so outlandishly that disapproval of my actions becomes the one thing both sides can agree on.</li> <li>In combat, 3 of my characters have at some point tried to browbeat their foe into submission as a Withering attack.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T11:14:25-08:00","id":1361527,"title":"","content":"I don't play enough (usually I'm a ST), but most of my characters have a &quot;monk&quot;-style to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T13:32:03-08:00","id":1361552,"title":"","content":"All my characters are sorcerers.<br /> Most of them are martial artists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T19:09:14-08:00","id":1361646,"title":"","content":"<ul><li>WLW and/or ace women.</li> <li>Scarring and/or a missing eye, often presented as adding to a character's visual appeal.</li> <li>Involvement in the criminal underworld, organized crime, etc.</li> <li>Usually social and/or mental over physical focus. Bureaucracy often.</li> <li>Guilt or regret.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T20:07:30-08:00","id":1361649,"title":"","content":"Note that these aren\u2019t things I <i>always</i> do, but things that show up fairly often.<br /> <br /> \u2022Brawl dots.<br /> \u2022Presence dots.<br /> \u2022Often my character holds no special reverence for any particular god or gods.<br /> \u2022I prefer them to be somewhat fresh-faced. Mostly because I want to see where life takes them. <br /> \u2022I tend to pick Intimacies that I know are going to be challenged in some way. A moral code, a selfish desire, a deep hatred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-17T23:42:22-08:00","id":1361674,"title":"","content":"All of my characters are big buffed hot gay men, tend to be overdesigned (which I'm trying to remedy), and oozing feminine energy. Plus none of them have archery or thrown as their main combat schtick it seems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T00:24:41-08:00","id":1361679,"title":"","content":"Most of my characters have deep social disabilities who don\u00b4t let them socialize and intimate at a personal level. Maybe they are overtly narcissistic (like my mortal sorceress) highly traumatized and paranoid (my Solar brawler) or just someone who see people as interchangeable tools (my Changing Moon revolutionary).My current Dragon Blooded bounty hunter is an explicit exception, being caring and honourable (and being mostly a female gunslinging Sanjuro).<br /> <br /> It\u00b4s weird. I like social characters, and this only happens to me when I play Exalted. My last Aquelarre character (which was the last non-Exalted character I played) was highly caring and functional, and my last Mage char was the kind girl in a group of harsher people. But whenever I play Exalted, my characters just end being jerks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I also always have to find an excuse to have Lore 3+. I don\u00b4t know, there is something simply cathartic about being able to Establish Facts, even if you never do it. Just knowing you have the possibility... <br /> <br /> I like to use athletic women, who fight (if they are fighters) with a close combat style, either unarmed or with weapons. The exception is my sorceress, who is pretty plump.<br /> <br /> Most of my characters are well dressed unless their background doesn\u00b4t allow for it (the Solar Brawler was a poor urchin, and she only had her travelling clothes, and a simple plain dress, who an old man gifted to her and she took a great care of it)<br /> <br /> I never play men*, but this have an easy explanation: I\u00b4m a transwoman, and had to pretend I was a man for more than twenty years. I won\u00b4t do it again. If the campaign setup only allow men (like the Warhammer campaigns ran by my old GM\u00b4d) I will play one to not be left out, but I\u00b4m pretty uncomfortable doing it..<br /> <br /> *My Lunar is an &quot;exception&quot;. She is currently in the male body she has stolen, mostly because he is a minor noble with a comfortable life she can use for her nefarious plans. I spend a big percentage of play time in male forms, but I don\u00b4t see it as playing a men, but a woman wearing a mask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T03:17:51-08:00","id":1361701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361494-what-s-on-your-exalted-bingo-card?p=1361527#post1361527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't play enough (usually I'm a ST), but most of my characters have a &quot;monk&quot;-style to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can still express personal preferences as a Storyteller, I know I do. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-18T19:58:52-08:00","id":1361837,"title":"","content":"Tiny Child<br /> Usually super strong<br /> Tanky.<br /> Usually a freedom fighter of some sort if celestial,<br /> Immaculate monk if terrestrial<br /> Almost always a nice good person. (Good isn't boring!)<br /> exceptions occur of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T01:09:34-08:00","id":1361869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1361494-what-s-on-your-exalted-bingo-card?p=1361701#post1361701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can still express personal preferences as a Storyteller, I know I do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then, as a ST I guess these are quite recurrent :<br /> <br /> - My NPCs that hold power are usually female, very strict and accept compromise only if it goes their way (Thanks mum and grandma ...)<br /> - I have no bad guys. All my guys are bad because something bad happened to them. I have the utmost difficulty to depict guys that are bad because they are.<br /> - I always give too much to my players to care for, for every problem they solve, twice more appear, and then complain that they don't have enough time to take an ellipse. I really need to slow down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T02:07:19-08:00","id":1361873,"title":"","content":"Thinking a bit on this but I have certain trends I think.<br /> <br /> -Social sorts in some fashion<br /> -Nobility in some way<br /> -Lean towards good guy hero sorts<br /> -Educated<br /> -At least appearance 3, I like to be pretty","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/BogMod\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/BogMod</a> I play a lot of videogames.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/131-bogmod","name":"BogMod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T02:42:56-08:00","id":1361875,"title":"","content":"ST and sometimes player. <br /> <br /> *Named character after a flower<br /> *Lunars tend to be women<br /> *A preference to fancy clothes<br /> *Massive Swol Bois<br /> *Pure Bastard Smooth Talkers<br /> *Slouch on throne<br /> *Villains aren't really villainous<br /> *(Lowkey making a lot of sense)<br /> *Lots of Languages","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T03:35:04-08:00","id":1361883,"title":"","content":"Let's see here...<ul><li>Criminal activity or association.</li> <li>Being okay with the status quo.</li> <li>Odd pets (god-blooded creatures, spirits, <i>a snail</i>).</li> <li><i>Occult dots.</i></li> <li>Unlikely friendships, often with abrasive or wicked people.</li> <li>Aesthetically, a touch of the sinister or monstrous (particularly in the anima).</li> <li>A limited colour palette.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}